WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.080
A celebration of the studio's&nbsp;
100-year animation legacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.440
Disney's "Wish" is finally in theaters,&nbsp;
and is a typically charming love letter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:14.920
to all-things-Disney. Want to know more about&nbsp;
that magical ending? Your wish is our command.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.880
"Wish" begins with a traditional storybook&nbsp;
opening. The narrator starts the tale by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:25.120
telling the story of Magnifico, the king, and his&nbsp;
queen, Amaya, who founded the kingdom of Rosas.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.120
Magnifico studied magic and was the one person in&nbsp;
Rosas who could grant wishes, so the people give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.040
him their biggest wish on their 18th birthday&nbsp;
with the understanding that they could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.160
granted by him at some point. In the meantime,&nbsp;
they forget the wish they gave to Magnifico.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.600
Asha, a 17-year-old girl, is interviewing&nbsp;
to be the King's Apprentice. She seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.640
impress him until she realizes that&nbsp;
he won't grant most of the wishes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.334
including her 100-year-old grandfather's,&nbsp;
because he judges them to be too dangerous.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:56.160
Asha tries to tell her grandfather about what&nbsp;
happened, but because it involves telling him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.920
his wish, he gets upset and tells her she's&nbsp;
excused from the family's dinner table. Asha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.480
runs out of the house and wishes upon a star,&nbsp;
and the star comes down from the sky and starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.640
granting the animals' and plants' wishes,&nbsp;
including that of Asha's goat, Valentino.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.960
"I'm talking. I am talking. Ha! Who&nbsp;
knew my voice would be this low?"

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.360
During this time, Magnifico sees the bright light&nbsp;
of the star and feels threatened. He calls a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.520
meeting to inform the citizens that they should&nbsp;
tell him if they know anything about the light,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.280
and the citizens start questioning him for&nbsp;
the first time. While this is happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:33.040
Asha sneaks up to the king's study to take&nbsp;
back her grandfather and mother's wishes.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.680
Asha heads home and gives&nbsp;
her grandfather's wish back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.800
but then Magnifico, who has started using&nbsp;
dark magic, appears. He knows she's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.360
one who wished upon the star and he means to&nbsp;
make her pay. She and her family escape in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.640
rowboat, but not before he crushes Asha's&nbsp;
mother's wish, making her feel deeply sad.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.680
Magnifico calls another meeting of the&nbsp;
kingdom where he introduces his informant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.720
Asha's only friend who's over 18, Simon.&nbsp;
He has his wish to be a knight granted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.720
but then becomes the king's pawn.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.960
Asha, Valentino, and Star return to&nbsp;
the city from the rowboat and join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.920
with her friends to take on the king.&nbsp;
The queen appears and joins them. Asha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.280
leads Magnifico away while the rest of&nbsp;
them go to get their wishes. But when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:17.000
Magnifico finally catches up with Asha,&nbsp;
it turns out it was Simon in disguise.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.240
Magnifico is still in the castle, and&nbsp;
while Amaya and Asha's friends manage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.360
to gather the wishes with Star's help,&nbsp;
Magnifico captures Star and traps it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.360
his staff. Asha runs to the castle to stop&nbsp;
this but Magnifico disarms her with magic.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.960
She appeals to the people of Rosas, and as&nbsp;
they make wishes, they overcome Magnifico&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.480
and he gets trapped in his own staff. Star is&nbsp;
freed and everyone can now pursue their wishes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.680
as they see fit. Simon apologizes to Asha,&nbsp;
and Asha becomes everyone's fairy godmother.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.760
Asha wishing on a star ended up inspiring&nbsp;
others, and eventually the whole kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.040
to rise up. It's a compelling statement&nbsp;
about the power that one simple act can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.640
have to convince others to take a stand&nbsp;
and help both themselves and others.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.000
Magnifico seems to be a benevolent king,&nbsp;
so people give him their wishes because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.320
one, he promises to safeguard them, and two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:10.000
because of the possibility that he'll grant&nbsp;
them. In Rosas, people don't wish upon stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.800
so in order to have their wish come&nbsp;
true, Magnifico is their only option.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.640
The trouble is that once they give their&nbsp;
wishes to Magnifico, they forget all about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.280
them. This means if there's a possibility that&nbsp;
their wish could be fulfilled through things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.040
like lessons or hard work, they can't pursue&nbsp;
that, because they don't remember their wishes.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.360
For example, Asha's grandfather wants to&nbsp;
inspire people by playing the mandolin, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.560
through lessons and frequent practice, he could&nbsp;
get good enough to inspire people. But because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.760
he surrendered his wish at 18 and can't remember&nbsp;
it, he's done nothing to pursue his wish since.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.280
While Magnifico tells the people that&nbsp;
giving up their wishes is a great thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.800
especially because he might grant them at&nbsp;
some point, in reality, it's a tragedy.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.080
"People come here because they&nbsp;
know they can't make their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.720
dreams come true. The journey&nbsp;
is too hard. It is too unfair."

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.000
Magnifico grants a lot of wishes, but he doesn't&nbsp;
grant everyone's wish, and that is by design.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.880
While there are some acceptable wishes that slip&nbsp;
through the cracks because he simply doesn't get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:08.560
to them, there are many more that he doesn't&nbsp;
grant because he judges them to be too risky.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.880
For instance, they could promote anarchy or&nbsp;
treason, or they could promote a smear campaign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.120
against Magnifico, or they could do neither&nbsp;
of those things and be completely innocent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.880
but since Magnifico doesn't know for&nbsp;
sure, he doesn't grant those wishes.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.160
Asha's grandfather is, again, a perfect example.&nbsp;
His desire to inspire people with his mandolin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.760
is deemed too vague to be granted. So&nbsp;
although it's a beautiful wish to Asha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.120
it has the potential to be sinister&nbsp;
to Magnifico, because he can imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:38.440
a scenario where Asha's grandfather's&nbsp;
music inspires people in negative ways.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.600
Because Magnifico has all the wishes and no one&nbsp;
else can even remember them, he and he alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:49.000
has the power to judge each person's wish,&nbsp;
granting only the ones he finds innocuous.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.636
"They deserve more than—"

00:04:50.636 --> 00:04:53.516
"I DECIDE WHAT EVERYONE DESERVES!"

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.760
Asha is perhaps the only person in Rosas who&nbsp;
would wish upon a star, and it has everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:02.600
to do with her father. Her father was deeply&nbsp;
invested in the stars and often took her to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:08.000
tree out over the water that allowed them to look&nbsp;
at the stars uninterrupted by the sights of Rosas.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.720
Asha learned from her father that everyone&nbsp;
is connected to the stars and took that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.880
perspective to heart, especially&nbsp;
because he died when she was 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.825
making his observations all&nbsp;
the more precious to her.

00:05:17.825 --> 00:05:21.120
She wishes upon the star because of her&nbsp;
father saying they're all connected to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.640
stars. She doesn't expect anything to happen&nbsp;
because of it, and is surprised when it does.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:30.320
In fact, when she makes her wish, which she states&nbsp;
in the song "This Wish," she simply wants everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.640
in Rosas to, quote, "have something more...&nbsp;
than this." More specifically, she wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.960
give her grandfather and mother's wishes back&nbsp;
to them, so they can work on them themselves.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.440
She sees this as better than waiting&nbsp;
for them to be granted by Magnifico,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.280
especially because he's already stated that&nbsp;
he will never grant her grandfather's wish.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.160
"Your wish will never be granted!"

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.280
When Asha states her wish, the&nbsp;
star she wishes on comes down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.400
Earth to be by her side as she tries to&nbsp;
right the wrongs of Magnifico. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.880
it doesn't grant Asha's wish. Jennifer Lee,&nbsp;
the co-writer of "Wish," told Rotten Tomatoes,

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:07.360
"Star really is all those things that Disney&nbsp;
gives us: hope, possibility, wonder, joy."

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.320
"That doesn't tell you the answers, it's&nbsp;
just there for you when you need it."

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.960
So Star isn't there to make Asha's&nbsp;
dream come true. It's there, instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.480
to offer hope and back her up when she needs it.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:21.160
This can be seen by the way Star accompanies&nbsp;
Asha when she breaks into Magnifico's study&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.520
and takes back her grandfather's wish.&nbsp;
It helps them get out of the locked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:28.280
elevator to the castle, for example,&nbsp;
by using its magic to unlock the door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.240
but Asha has to do the heavy lifting of&nbsp;
taking her grandfather's wish herself.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.000
That said, there are times when Star can&nbsp;
make wishes come true. It does this for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.320
many of the animals and plants in the forest,&nbsp;
sprinkling them with stardust so they can talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.000
and therefore granting their wishes. Star also&nbsp;
makes the wishes float out of the castle so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:51.040
the people can reclaim them. So Star does&nbsp;
have the ability to help, to some extent.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:54.040
In the end, Asha, through her&nbsp;
kindness and selflessness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.160
has managed to free the whole kingdom from&nbsp;
the tyranny of Magnifico. While Amaya,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:01.880
the queen, has become the ruler of the&nbsp;
kingdom, Asha is anointed the kingdom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.240
fairy godmother by Star, who gives her&nbsp;
a wand and robes in a ceremony that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.040
very much like that in "Cinderella" when&nbsp;
Cinderella gets her gown for the ball.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.480
Asha objects to the new role, which&nbsp;
is exactly why she'll be good at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:17.480
according to her friends. But granting&nbsp;
wishes exactly as a fairy godmother would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:21.880
makes it seem like she's pretty much replacing&nbsp;
Magnifico, given he was doing the same thing.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.880
Asha promises to be just about it, and that&nbsp;
seems to be enough for the people of Rosas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:30.920
but it's hard not to wonder if Asha will stick&nbsp;
to that sentiment. After all, she's only 17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:34.960
she has a lot of life to live and the power&nbsp;
to grant wishes has the power to corrupt her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.880
just like it did Magnifico.
Actors react

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:42.480
Ariana DeBose is excited to be part of "Wish,"&nbsp;
voicing Asha. She's a longtime Disney fan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.840
so to come to the film that is being put&nbsp;
out as part of Disney's 100th is a special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.240
honor. When asked what audiences can take away&nbsp;
from the film, DeBose told The Nerds of Color,

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.520
"In this particular film, to watch this young girl&nbsp;
of color, with braids and freckles, an unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:00.440
leader, step into her power. It doesn’t mean that&nbsp;
she’s not afraid; she is. And it doesn’t mean that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:05.400
she doesn’t make mistakes; she does. But to see&nbsp;
how one person can step up to the plate and say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.880
‘I’m not really sure how I’m going to get my&nbsp;
way through, but I’m going to get through.’"

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.400
Chris Pine, like DeBose, was tickled to be&nbsp;
part of "Wish," voicing Magnifico. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.800
especially thrilled to be voicing&nbsp;
the villain, telling Kim Holcomb,

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:21.360
"There's humor to it, the guy's a buffoon&nbsp;
[...] I think I like playing characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.040
that think they're really, really cool and&nbsp;
simply aren't when you get underneath the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:29.280
hood. It's always fun to play those guys.&nbsp;
Even his hero song, 'This Is the Thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.520
I Get' is the most revealing song about&nbsp;
his deep insecurities about being loved."

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.800
Pine also had many complimentary&nbsp;
things to say about his co-star and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.760
the chemistry they shared.&nbsp;
Pine told Today's Esquire,

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.840
"Working with Ariana was an absolute&nbsp;
delight. She's not only an incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.280
talented performer but also a wonderful&nbsp;
person. Our chemistry on set translated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:53.240
seamlessly onto the screen, and&nbsp;
I'm grateful for the experience."

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.480
Jennifer Lee has been part of some&nbsp;
of the greatest animated films of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:00.520
last fifteen years, including "Frozen,"&nbsp;
which she co-directed. She also co-wrote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.360
the screenplay for "Wish," and spoke&nbsp;
about Asha to Rotten Tomatoes, saying,

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:08.000
"We were talking about Asha and knowing we&nbsp;
wanted that moment as a teenager where you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.160
living your life, everything's fine,&nbsp;
and then all the sudden you're like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:14.200
'Hey, that's not right.' And I&nbsp;
always say it's a very generous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:18.000
time. Teenagers are the ones who want&nbsp;
to make the world better for others."

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.120
"We give them a bad rap sometimes,&nbsp;
that they're selfish, and I'm like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.600
'They're the ones who can see a better world."

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.840
Peter Del Veccho, a veteran&nbsp;
producer of Disney animated films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.083
has a lot to say about the&nbsp;
villain, telling Comicbook.com,

00:09:30.083 --> 00:09:33.120
"Disney villains have evolved over&nbsp;
time, and some villains are revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.480
but there's something delicious about&nbsp;
knowing that someone's the villain from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.680
the beginning. What makes this one&nbsp;
unique is he's also charming and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.767
charismatic and you actually watch him&nbsp;
evolve as more pressure is put on him."

